WEBVTT

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.140
Thank you for the meal!

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:15.640
And so...

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.010
I'll be...

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.310
Leaving now!

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.900
Fuji-nee sure is in a rush this morning.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.160
Yes, she said she needs to prepare for her class.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.090
You're amazing, Senpai.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.510
Well then, Senpai, I'll be going on ahead today, all right?

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.520
Hey, Rider, is something up with Sakura?

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.060
Well, yes.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:07.980
Actually, it's nothing you need to worry about.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.940
If you say so, Rider.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.610
Yes, I think she'll be fine.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:20.890
Issei.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.520
Reikan, what is it?

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:30.060
I'd like you to take these to Shirou.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.440
Ah, that's...

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.160
Emiya.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.200
Good morning, Issei.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.870
Good morning. I was just looking for you.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.580
You wanted to see me?

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.380
Yes. Look at this.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:58.180
Um, they look like bamboo shoots.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.760
Because they are bamboo shoots.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.180
They were given to Reikan,

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.770
and he wanted to give you a share,
to thank you for those sandwiches.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.320
No need to thank me.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.690
But thanks. Everyone will be thrilled.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.490
You'll need to soak them first,
but you probably know that, Emiya.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.540
All right, see you later.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.870
Maybe I'll bring him some in a box lunch sometime.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:36.340
<i>Bamboo shoots, huh? How should we have these?</i>

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.840
<i>Bamboo shoot rice, perhaps?</i>

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.430
<i>Boiled or grilled?</i>

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:43.850
Emiya?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.890
Why do you have bamboo shoots?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.190
Oh, Issei gave them to me.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.650
The president dug up bamboo shoots?

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.420
Matou?

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.300
Mitsuru-senpai.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:23.430
Shopping with Rider?

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.350
Yes.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:30.310
Are you doing your shopping for the week?

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:34.860
What? Oh no, this is for tonight's dinner.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.070
Everything tastes better when you make a lot, right?

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:41.110
And it's more interesting when
you add a lot of ingredients.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.700
So what are you making tonight?

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.870
The menu?

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.210
I thought I'd make gratin tonight.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.960
Gratin, huh? Sounds great!

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:59.510
It's simple, but a home staple.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.720
And you can cook up a lot at once.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.930
All right, Matou.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:07.600
I'll be on my way,
since someone's waiting for me at home!

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.060
Okay. See you tomorrow at school.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.390
Right, see you!

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:22.780
Sis, are you done shopping? Let's go home already.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:23.780
Right, right.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.910
Why don't we make gratin, too?

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:29.580
Okay.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.370
Senpai?

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.670
For today...

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.500
I thought that we'd have gratin.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.170
The kind you make with stew mix.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:48.640
Gratin, huh? Sounds good. I'll help.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.640
Let me get the oven out.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.060
Thank you very much.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.270
Um, Senpai?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.400
Huh? What's up?

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.900
I thought it might be kind of
boring to make gratin the usual way.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.950
Hmm, I guess so.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.880
Sakura, how about adding these?

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.340
Bamboo shoots?

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.800
Issei gave them to me this morning,
and I've soaked them in water.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.390
I'm glad I only had morning class today.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.230
If we don't get started right away, they'll taste bitter.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.190
We could boil them in water.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.860
But you know, raw bamboo shoots taste best fresh.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:43.230
Though it is a lot of work.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:47.070
Bamboo shoot gratin, huh?

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:49.160
I've never heard of that before.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.240
It's my first time, too.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.450
But I'm sure it'll taste amazing.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.540
Well then, shall we begin?

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.170
Yes.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:06.090
Slice the bamboo shoots thinly,
about the size of macaroni.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.720
Slice the onions thinly as well.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:10.800
The chicken breast should be bite-size.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:16.770
Use a peeler to peel away the hard root of the asparagus,

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:20.230
boil in salted hot water, al dente,

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:23.820
then put them in ice water
and chop into manageable slices.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.900
Boil the macaroni in plenty of hot water.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.490
Pour oil into the frying pan,

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:36.500
fry the chicken breast, onions
and bamboo shoots in that order.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:42.580
Add the macaroni, water and milk.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:48.720
Add stew mix when it comes to a boil,
and adjust the flavor and viscosity.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:56.680
After placing in a heat-resistant plate,
top it off with the asparagus and cheese.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:01.270
Sprinkle some bread crumbs over to finish it off.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.730
And into the oven it goes!

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:12.360
All right, why don't we make a salad while we wait?

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.530
Oh, then I'll make some soup!

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:27.170
I can smell cheese, so yummy!

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.970
It's nice and brown on top.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.480
Okay, it's done!

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.310
Hey, it's gratin!

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.900
That's your specialty, huh, Sakura?

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.900
Looks so good!

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:56.990
Senpai came up with the idea
of changing the ingredients a bit.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.120
Now then...

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.080
Thanks for the meal!

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:27.150
The texture is amazing!

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:30.320
Yes. Bamboo shoots go well with it, huh?

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:35.660
This is what you brought home today, right?

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:36.820
Shaped like this?

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.540
That's right.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:42.200
Food tastes great when it's in season, huh?

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:47.630
Putting bamboo shoots into gratin.
What a nice touch, Shirou!

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.510
Um, Senpai?

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:58.050
Would you mind letting me
have some bamboo shoots, please?

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.770
Oh, sure. There's plenty.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:04.230
Thank you very much.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:15.400
Gratin, huh?

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:18.490
Not that I really like it.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.710
What's this? Bamboo shoots?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.510
Hmmm...

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:42.310
All right!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.680
Brother finished it all.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:49.710
I've got to hand it to Senpai.
I still have so much to learn from him!

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:52.900
The gratin you make is delicious, too, Sakura.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:56.700
I'll make sure he doesn't leave anything next time, too.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:58.200
You do that.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:10:59.870
Yes!
